Rule 1 (The output tensor's dtype should match the input tensor's dtype to avoid dtype mismatch errors.)
{input : tensor, out : tensor} |= dtype_(input) = dtype_(out)
>>
Rule 2 (Input tensor should not have a complex dtype to prevent 'sorting_kernel_method_name' not implemented errors.)
{input : tensor} |= (dtype_(input) ≠ 9) ∧ (dtype_(input) ≠ 10)
>>
Rule 3 (The input tensor should have at least one dimension to be sortable. Prevents errors that may arise from zero-dimensional tensors.)
{input : tensor} |= ndim(input) > 0
>>
Rule 5 (If out is provided, it should have the same data type as the input.)
{input : tensor, out : tensor} |= if out ≠ false then dtype_(input) = dtype_(out)
>>
Rule 9 (The number of dimensions of input tensor must be a reasonable number, e.g., less than 10.)
{input : tensor} |= ndim(input) < 10
>>
Rule 10 (Dtype should be one of the allowed values.)
{input : tensor} |= (dtype_(input) = 0) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 4) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 5) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(input) = 10)
